 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "Though, in a little walk by Sunday,\nThe maiden's moonlight mirrored her shadow;\nYet she hath not been to the halls away,\nFor 'tis no place for Dian below.\nAnd thus, while thou friendst with me agree,\nThou sayest that I am cool and cumbering me;\nThou art bounteous to my few sicknesse me,\nAnd thou hast nourished my suffering thee.\nBut how can pity be e'er appropriate\nTo me who ne're fail'd but once away?\nFor if they must stay, where are the places?\nNay, all happy what were their pleasure they!",
